---
// /what-we-treat/mental-health/adhd/: What-We-Treat-Content-Briefs.md §N. Sources in
// docs/content/what-we-treat-sources-mental.md. Rotation: Reviews only. Reviewed by Dana.
// Confirmed by the client (2026-09-22). Stimulants are not used during the program (Q3).
import ServicePage from '../../../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import NextSteps from '../../../components/NextSteps.astro';
import Icon from '../../../components/Icon.astro';
import { WWT, CATEGORIES, MENTAL_PAGES } from '../../../data/treat.js';
import { conditionAbout } from '../../../lib/programSchema.js';

const path = '/what-we-treat/mental-health/adhd/';

const signs = [
  'You use to slow a racing mind, or to feel able to focus',
  'Restlessness and impulsive choices keep leading back to using',
  'Routines fall apart quickly, and substances fill the gaps',
  'A stimulant prescription has become hard to use as directed',
];

const treating = [
  { icon: 'calendar', title: 'Structure and routine', text: 'Treatment happens at the same time, with the same facilitator and the same group. That predictable rhythm is part of the treatment.' },
  { icon: 'compass', title: 'Life skills and goal setting', text: 'Our groups cover life skills, goal setting, boundaries and emotional regulation: practical tools for the days that feel scattered.' },
  { icon: 'shield', title: 'Coping skills that stick', text: 'CBT and DBT coping skills give you something to reach for when impulses or frustration hit, other than a substance.' },
  { icon: 'refresh', title: 'Practice in real life', text: 'You go home every day and try what you learned. What worked, and what didn’t, comes back to group the next time.' },
];

const approaches = [
  { name: 'CBT', text: 'Helps with the thought patterns and habits that make follow-through hard and using feel like the answer.' },
  { name: 'DBT', text: 'Builds skills for emotional regulation and impulse control in the moment.' },
  { name: 'Internal Family Systems (IFS)', text: 'Explores the different parts of yourself, including the frustrated or self-critical ones that often come with ADHD.' },
  { name: 'Psychodynamic therapy', text: 'Looks at how experiences like feeling criticized or not good enough may still shape how you see yourself.' },
];

const faqs = [
  { q: 'Can I keep taking Adderall during the program?', a: 'No. Sunview is abstinence-based, and stimulant medications like Adderall aren’t used during the program. Your Telemed Clinix provider evaluates your needs and makes medication decisions that fit your treatment.' },
  { q: 'I have a prescription. Doesn’t that settle it?', a: 'A prescription doesn’t by itself determine whether outpatient care fits. During pre-screening we look at what you take, how much, how often and for how long, so we can recommend a level of care that’s safe for you.' },
  { q: 'Do I need an ADHD diagnosis to start?', a: 'No. You don’t need a specific diagnosis to reach out. Your pre-screening and assessment help us understand the full picture, and psychiatric evaluation is part of the program through Telemed Clinix.' },
  { q: 'Do you treat ADHD without substance use?', a: 'Our programs are built for people living with substance use and co-occurring mental health conditions together. If ADHD is your only concern, call us anyway and we’ll help you find the right kind of care.' },
  { q: 'Which program should I start in?', a: 'Our Clinical Director reviews your pre-screening and recommends a level of care using ASAM criteria and clinical judgment. <a href="/programs/">Compare PHP, IOP and OP</a>.' },
];
---
<ServicePage
  path={path}
  metaTitle="ADHD and Addiction Treatment in West Palm Beach | Sunview"
  description="ADHD treated alongside substance use in West Palm Beach: structure, skills and psychiatric care in PHP, IOP and OP, with no stimulant medications."
  crumbs={[WWT, { name: CATEGORIES.mental.name, href: CATEGORIES.mental.href }, { name: 'ADHD', href: path }]}
  h1="ADHD and Addiction Treatment in West Palm Beach"
  subheading="Structure, skills and support that work with how your mind works."
  lead="ADHD treated alongside substance use in outpatient PHP, IOP and OP, with a predictable routine, practical skills groups and psychiatric care, without stimulant medications during the program."
  faqTitle="Frequently Asked Questions About ADHD Treatment"
  faqs={faqs}
  reviews
  about={conditionAbout('Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder')}
>
  {/* The cycle */}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_0.9fr]">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">The cycle</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">How ADHD and Substance Use Feed Each Other</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Looking for focus, finding a new problem</p>
        <div class="prose-sv mt-6">
          <p>At Sunview, ADHD is treated as part of <a href="/what-we-treat/dual-diagnosis/">dual diagnosis treatment</a>, alongside substance use, within our Partial Hospitalization, Intensive Outpatient and Outpatient programs.</p>
          <p>For many people, substances start as a way to manage what ADHD makes hard: a mind that won’t slow down, restlessness, frustration, or trouble focusing. Some use to feel calmer; others use stimulants to feel able to function. The relief doesn’t last, and using adds new problems of its own.</p>
          <p>None of this is a character flaw. We look at how your attention, your emotions and your substance use connect, and build a plan that works with how your mind works.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      {/* REVIEW 8.5: plain-language passage pending Elizabeth review */}
      <aside class="card self-start !p-7">
        <h3 class="text-xl">Signs the two may be connected</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          {signs.map((s) => <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check" class="mt-1 h-4 w-4 shrink-0 text-teal" />{s}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Treating it at Sunview */}
  <section class="section bg-mist">
    <div class="container-x">
      <div class="max-w-5xl">
        <span class="eyebrow">At Sunview</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Treating ADHD Alongside Addiction at Sunview</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Structure is part of the treatment</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        {treating.map((t) => (
          <div class="card">
            <Icon name={t.icon} class="h-7 w-7 text-teal" />
            <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl">{t.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2">{t.text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Therapies */}
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container-x grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr]">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Therapy</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Therapy Approaches We Use</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Practical tools, plus the story underneath</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg">Skills help with the day-to-day. Many adults with ADHD also carry years of being told they weren’t trying hard enough. We make room for that too.</p>
        <a href="/therapies/" class="btn-teal mt-8">How therapy works at Sunview <Icon name="arrow" /></a>
      </div>
      <dl class="divide-y divide-line self-start rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-line">
        {approaches.map((a) => (
          <div class="grid gap-1 p-6 sm:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] sm:gap-6">
            <dt class="font-extrabold">{a.name}</dt>
            <dd>{a.text}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* Psychiatry */}
  <section class="section bg-mist">
    <div class="container-x grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Medication</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-[2.1875rem]">Psychiatric Care and Medication</h2>
        <p class="subheading mt-3">Medication decisions made by your provider, with care</p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg">Sunview is abstinence-based, so stimulant medications like Adderall and similar aren’t used during the program. That doesn’t mean you’re on your own: psychiatric evaluation and medication management are part of every program through our partner, Telemed Clinix.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg">Your provider reviews your history and current medications and decides what’s clinically appropriate while you’re in treatment. Appointments happen virtually from a private office at Sunview, and you can keep the same provider after you finish.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card !p-8">
        <Icon name="pill" class="h-8 w-8 text-teal" />
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-xl">What psychiatric care includes</h3>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal" />Psychiatric evaluation and medication review</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal" />Appointments scheduled for you, on site</li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icon name="check-circle" class="mt-0.5 h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-teal" />The same provider after discharge, if you want</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/programs/psychiatry-medication-management/" class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-bold text-teal underline decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-teal-light">Psychiatric care and medication management <Icon name="arrow" class="h-4 w-4" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextSteps
    class="section"
    title="Which Level of Care Fits"
    subtitle="Our Clinical Director helps you decide"
    level={`<p>Many people start in the <a href="/programs/php/">Partial Hospitalization Program</a>, where the same schedule every weekday builds routine. The <a href="/programs/iop/">Intensive Outpatient Program</a>, day or evening, fits when you need depth and have to keep working. The <a href="/programs/outpatient/">Outpatient Program</a> keeps a weekly anchor in place as your routine gets stronger.</p>`}
    related={[
      { label: 'Co-occurring mental health treatment', href: CATEGORIES.mental.href },
      ...MENTAL_PAGES.filter((p) => p.href !== path).map((p) => ({ label: p.label, href: p.href })),
      { label: 'Dual diagnosis treatment', href: CATEGORIES.dual.href },
      { label: 'Substance use disorder treatment', href: CATEGORIES.substance.href },
    ]}
  />
</ServicePage>
